# Template for local environment configuration.
# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in real values, or export these in your shell.
# NEVER put real secrets in this file — it is committed.

# ---- Required in every non-test environment ----
# The application refuses to start without this. There is no fallback default:
# a committed default would let dev and staging run on a public secret.
# Must be at least 256 bits (32+ chars) for HS256.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 48
JWT_SECRET=

# ---- Local dev database ----
# Required — application-dev.yml has no fallback for these either.
DB_USERNAME=
DB_PASSWORD=

# ---- Google Sheets sync ----
# Leave LESUCCESS_SHEETS_ENABLED unset (or false) to keep the integration off.
# Setting it to true activates GoogleSheetsConfig, which then REQUIRES a spreadsheet
# id AND one of the two credential sources below — supplying neither fails startup
# with an error naming the missing variable, rather than silently skipping the sync.
#
# Credentials, in priority order (base64 wins when both are set):
#   SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_BASE64 — base64-encoded service account JSON, decoded in
#                               memory and never written to disk. Use in production.
#   SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_PATH   — path to the key file. Local dev convenience only;
#                               do not bake this file into a Docker image.
#
# On naming: the unprefixed names below are the literal ${...} placeholders in
# application.yml. The LESUCCESS_-prefixed forms (LESUCCESS_SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_BASE64,
# LESUCCESS_SHEETS_SPREADSHEET_ID, ...) ALSO work and in fact take precedence, because
# relaxed binding maps them onto the lesuccess.sheets.* properties and environment
# variables outrank application.yml. Either form is fine; don't set both to different
# values, since the prefixed one silently wins.
LESUCCESS_SHEETS_ENABLED=
SHEETS_SPREADSHEET_ID=
# Generate with:  base64 -w0 path/to/service-account.json
SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_BASE64=
SHEETS_CREDENTIALS_PATH=
   